WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.643
Cricket,

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.693
a quiet sport.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.473
Pioneered by the British.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.983
Measured, considered, timeless.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.110
Just a couple of decades ago,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.870
cricket was struggling
to attract audiences

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.873
and its commercial future
was very much in doubt.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.070
Now, it has the second
biggest sporting franchise

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.223
in the world, bettered only by the NFL.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.120
At the center of its
success is one country

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.302
and its record breaking tournament,

00:00:56.302 --> 00:00:58.023
the Indian Premier League.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.050
So there's been a revolution in cricket.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.030
Traditionally what used to happen,

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.890
when English cricket started,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.930
cricket in the rest of the world stopped.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.110
Now, such is the glamor of IPL,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.900
such are the riches the IPL provides

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.293
that English cricket has
to bow down to India.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.500
There are 74 games now in the IPL

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.030
and each one is valued at over

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.430
10 million pounds for one game.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.940
There's no way that other
formats of the game before

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.830
could have commanded that sort of

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.620
financial power or value.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.050
The figures that are talked about is that

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.690
80% of world cricket's income

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.330
is provided by India in
one form or the other.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.170
India currently has a population
of 1.4 billion people.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.860
IPL has a viewership of
almost 700 million people.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.690
Worldwide fanbase for cricket

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.520
is about two and a half billion people.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.090
We are 27% of that total
fan base worldwide.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.933
So potential to grow this
viewership? Immense, massive.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.630
This is the story of how

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.700
one country became the driving force

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.273
behind the biggest sporting
turnaround of the 21st century.

00:02:20.555 --> 00:02:23.550
Well, cricket is this unique English game.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.460
The English invented most of the sports,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.340
but cricket is probably unique in that

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.180
the two sets of players
are doing opposite things.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.210
One of them is playing with a bat

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.373
and the other one is playing with a ball.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.850
It's one of those kind
of quiet enigmatic sports

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.170
to describe, I think.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.030
It's the battle between runs,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.830
the number of runs you can score

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.150
versus the number of wickets.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.920
And a wicket is when a batter gets out

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.653
and so it's a contest
between runs and wickets.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.850
The overall aim of the game

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.493
is to score more runs
than the opposing team.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.360
A run is essentially a point
and it's given every time

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.910
a batter runs between the wickets,

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.000
which is possible after
the ball has been bowled.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.040
Four runs are given if
the batsman hits the ball

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.510
beyond the boundary of the pitch,

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.310
with the ball having hit the ground.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.940
A six is given for batters
who can clear the boundary

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.740
without the ball hitting the ground.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.220
The fielding team bowls
to the batting team.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.650
A fielder bowls in sets of six balls,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.240
which are called an over.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.000
After each over, the bowler changes.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.730
The best way to prevent the
batting team from scoring

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.940
is by getting the batsman
out or taking wickets.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.500
This can be done in many ways:

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.410
bowling, catching, or running out.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.720
Once 10 of the 11 batsmen are out,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.230
their innings finishes and
they can't score anymore runs.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.420
The same is true if they run out of time,

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.270
which varies depending on
the type of cricket game

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.920
and is where the most revolution

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.083
has taken place in recent years.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.640
Its most traditional format
is multi-day cricket,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.600
so where it's played with a red ball

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.270
and there are

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.700
three results possible:
win, lose, or draw.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.530
So I know people are completely stumped

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.910
by the fact that you can play a game

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.283
for five days and still
draw at the end of it.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.330
Cricket's complicated
rules and long playtime

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.980
meant it struggled to appeal to fans

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.810
outside Commonwealth countries

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.660
who had deeply historical
ties to the game.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.940
Invented in England in the 1600s,

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.980
cricket arrived in
other parts of the globe

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.440
during the late 17th and 18th centuries

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.780
via British colonizers.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.410
The British took the game to
different parts of the world,

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.770
as they expanded, as they
went in search of trade,

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.780
and then they acquired territories.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.380
They didn't tell people
you have to play our sport.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.020
They played their sport
and the other people,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.340
seeing the British play the
sport, was attracted by it.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.990
While a number of the
Commonwealth countries

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.850
adopted the game as their own,

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.763
one managed to turn the
sport into big business.

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.900
I think the Indians, who have
been given no chance at all,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.760
are likely to give a
great deal more trouble

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:03.963
than many people expect.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:09.090
When I was a very young boy,
that was a long time ago,

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.980
in the fifties, as a five year old,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.440
I was taken in India, in Mumbai,

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.340
to watch England play India.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.820
Mihir Bose, the BBC's
first sports news editor,

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.310
is one of cricket's
best known commentators.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.797
His most recent book, "Nine
Waves: The Extraordinary Story

00:05:26.797 --> 00:05:28.980
of How India Took Over the Cricket World"

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.220
traces the country's rise
from colonial dependency

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.590
to global dominance within the sport.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.250
The money in cricket came
through, and this was worldwide,

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.490
came through people at
the gates buying tickets.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.490
When a team came over
in England, Australia,

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.760
West Indies, New Zealand, or whoever,

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.900
there would be in the cities,
what was called test fever.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.490
People would want to buy tickets,

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.899
there would be long queues
to get tickets and so on

00:05:56.899 --> 00:05:59.924
and that was the situation

00:05:59.924 --> 00:06:04.800
'til well into the 1990s.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.810
Television had shown
its potential in India

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.360
during the 1982 Asian Games,

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.370
but it wasn't until the 1990s

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.040
when domestic viewership
reached critical mass

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.440
that its full potential
could be capitalized on.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.430
The cricket authorities in India realized

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:23.820
television stations were
prepared to pay big money.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.750
By then, crowds had
declined all over the world.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.370
People were watching on television

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.460
and English cricket and
Australian cricket found

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.470
that when they played India,

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.750
they could sell their
television rights to these

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.450
Indian television stations
for a lot of money.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.640
And that is where India, if you like,

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.023
took over the world game.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.940
While the sports original days long format

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.120
continued to have an appeal
with longstanding fans,

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.020
cricket struggled to entice
new, younger audiences.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.840
This pressure only intensified
as the unparalleled

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.020
popularity of mega franchises like the NFL

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.260
and the EPL continued to proliferate.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.600
In an attempt to reinvigorate the sport,

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:10.413
a variety of shorter formats
with fewer overs were created.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.050
England, finding audiences
were not coming to cricket,

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.330
spectators were not coming to cricket,

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.550
devised a new format of the game

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:23.520
where only 20 overs were
bowled by each side.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.110
You know, shorten the game

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.630
because then you could play
the game in an English summer,

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.120
start at one or two o'clock,

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.490
play 'til about seven
o'clock, eight o'clock,

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.490
and somebody could
finish their work at five

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.620
and just pop in for two or three hours.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:38.673
That was the idea.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.330
England's 20 over format,

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:45.150
also known as T20 or 20-20,

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.854
launched its first professional
tournaments in 2003.

00:07:48.854 --> 00:07:50.640
The shorter format made it

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.040
a much better fit for broadcasters.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.500
Sky Sports televised eight group matches

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.230
and the entirety of finals day live.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:01.500
England's T20 World Cup
was a success domestically

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.970
and had proved the potential

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.283
of a more explosive version of the game.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.510
But it would take a
total disruption in 2008

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.730
to change the course of cricket.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.367
And that disruptor came in the form

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.033
of the Indian Premier League.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.260
No matter which times on your end,

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.440
over the next 51 days, it's only one time.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.950
And that is to celebrate
cricket's biggest festival.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.383
Welcome to the Vivo Indian Premier League.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.040
They made it into a spectacle

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:41.220
and the old-fashioned
traditionalists find this abhorrent.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.090
To them, that's not cricket.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.730
Cricket is theater where, you know,

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.320
you have intellectual discussions

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.870
as to where the ball is
played and so on and so forth.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.760
Here they said, no, no,
you don't need all that.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.170
You want entertainment.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.830
You want to rival what
the cinema offers you,

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.443
what any other form of
entertainment offers you.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.620
The IPL didn't just take inspiration

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.100
from America's pre-show
entertainment and pyrotechnics.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.680
It also adopted a similar league structure

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.800
where the same teams compete every year.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.580
For the IPL, they devised
completely new teams.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.970
So it became Mumbai
Indians owned by one of the

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.100
richest businessmen in India,

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.500
composed some of them from Mumbai,

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.780
composed of players from around the world,

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:28.740
or the Chennai Super Kings, or you know,

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.330
the Kolkata Knight Riders.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.630
So they came up with these exotic names.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.610
You know, the one difference is

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.800
this is not about a country
playing another country.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.010
The one difference is you're
able to, as a franchise,

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.627
attract the best in an auction,

00:09:43.627 --> 00:09:46.260
which is done prior to
the season beginning,

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:48.600
where you bid for the
best players in the world

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.370
for a certain price tag.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.149
How much has the IPL, you know,

00:09:52.149 --> 00:09:55.050
changed the face of cricket
because of the money involved?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.146
Yeah, well, I mean the money involved

00:09:57.146 --> 00:09:59.490
is huge for the players these days.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.860
This is a time of upheaval in sport,

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.830
where new moneyed leagues
promising big payouts

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.440
threaten to upend the status quo.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.650
From Saudi Arabia's
controversial LIV golf tour

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.960
that saw golfers sign up despite concerns

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.120
over the country's human rights record

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.240
and then lose their place
from renowned PGA tours,

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.850
to the proposed European Super League,

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.220
a breakaway competition in football

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.670
designed to guarantee millions
of dollars for a select few

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.983
at the expense of long
established leagues.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:34.050
And the IPL is no different,
with only 10 teams competing,

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:36.960
each under owners with deep pockets.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.420
It quickly attracted the
world's best players,

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.520
causing issues for any other tournaments

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.250
that took place during the IPL season.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:48.030
Player choice, scheduling,
the kind of proliferation of

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.720
short format leagues whilst
also trying to schedule

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:54.570
international cricket, whether
it's test match cricket,

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.750
the domestic game, the
other international formats.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.440
You know, it is quite a
challenging jigsaw puzzle.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.970
The organization unofficially

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.830
in charge of putting that puzzle together

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.763
is the Board of Control for
Cricket in India, or the BCCI.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.150
While the International
Cricket Council is named

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.160
the global watchman, money,

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.833
as is often the case, wields power.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.980
The humble truth here is the BCCI

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.460
is the richest body today
in the world of cricket

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:24.750
across the globe.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.690
And I think it's purely
because of the success of IPL,

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.630
massively, so you've got
sponsorship deals coming,

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.180
pouring through every
single corner of the room

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.650
into the BCCI.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:38.550
80% of world cricket's
income is provided by India

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.990
in one form or the other.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.670
There's television rights,

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.550
there are commercial deals
when India play abroad,

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.080
if you look around the
stadiums, the marketing

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.470
of the sponsors names
are Indian sponsors names

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:53.910
because they have got the rights.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:56.790
They want their names on television

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.080
because Indians are watching

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.480
and therefore they'll sell the product.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:03.330
So the BCCI obviously
continues to, you know,

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.430
aggregate power in a sense purely because

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:08.490
of the type of consumers
it has at its disposal.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.890
The Indian consumer, like I said,

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.470
700 million people watching IPL,

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:16.350
which has probably the
least number of games

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:19.470
across any sporting, you
know, format across the world.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.750
I'm not just talking
cricket, I'm talking NFL,

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:25.110
I'm talking about MLB, I'm talking EPL.

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:26.760
This has the least number of games.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.260
It has the maximum viewership.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:32.640
The success of the

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.700
2022 IPL media rights e-auction

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.760
highlighted just how successful
this franchise has become

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.653
in such a short period of time.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:46.260
The TV and digital rights
for 2022 - 2027 matches

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.113
collectively sold for $6.2 billion.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.170
This not only reaffirmed the IPL

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.640
as the leading cricket league,

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.510
but also made it the second
most valuable league globally.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.150
At more than $13 million per match,

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:02.070
the IPL has surpassed global leagues

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:04.077
such as the EPL and the MLB

00:13:04.077 --> 00:13:06.393
and is second only to the NFL.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.930
Disney bagged the TV rights

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.670
and a joint venture between Paramount

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.100
and Mukesh Ambani's Reliance Industries,

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.110
won digital streaming rights.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.763
Media companies are constantly

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:19.920
working hard to make sure

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.600
they get the right form of content

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:26.600
such that the consumer loyalty
continues to stick and grow.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.370
If you look at the case of Netflix

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.260
in the two quarters that went by

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.530
they actually said they're
gonna come off massively

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:37.620
on their consumer numbers
only because, you know,

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.900
they're not able to penetrate
countries like India,

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.300
which require a different form of content.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.190
I'm not saying that they
should go after cricket

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:46.980
as a possible broadcasting thing.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:50.310
They may, who knows, but
if you get, you know,

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.800
sport which is universal, has no language,

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.230
something like a football or a cricket,

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.660
which actually attracts more consumers

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:01.050
given its religious following
in those specific countries,

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.870
I don't see a reason why you
will see more media companies

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.180
coming and you know,
trying to get a partnership

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.120
with the BCCI, given the
massive fan following

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:09.993
across the world.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.710
It's widely agreed upon that media

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.450
is what's propelled the values of teams

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.343
to such astronomical heights.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:21.600
In the US, the Big 10, a
college football conference,

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.550
just signed an $8
billion media rights deal

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:29.160
and Apple signed onto a 10
year global broadcast deal

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.253
to stream major league
soccer worth $250 million.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.600
With so much untapped revenue to play for,

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.630
a flurry of new T20
leagues are being created

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:43.053
in an attempt to ride the
wave of the IPL's success.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:45.720
South Africa have started fleshing out

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:48.090
details of the new T20 league.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.530
Players are already on board.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.630
A broadcast deal has been confirmed

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.610
and team owners revealed.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.590
SA's previous attempts that
getting an international

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.140
T20 league off the ground have failed.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.240
South Africa and the UAE

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:04.080
are both set to launch
new T20 leagues in 2023,

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:07.290
adding to an already
packed cricketing calendar.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.210
These tournaments will
put a further strain

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.460
on resources and talent,

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:14.730
especially as the current
ruling by the BCCI states

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.910
no Indian national player can
take part in other leagues

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.710
unless they permanently retire

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:21.933
from the IPL and national cricket.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.110
The thinking here is
that players competing

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:28.950
in other T20 tournaments will
take fans to those franchises

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:30.690
which could lead to tougher competition

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.060
in terms of attraction, attention,

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:35.100
and brand value for the IPL.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:39.450
So you see in T20 leagues, in Australia,

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:42.450
the Big Bash League, the
Caribbean Premier League,

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:45.990
one in England, and now two
new leagues being launched,

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.700
just announced, one in South Africa

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:50.190
and the other one in Dubai,
the Emirates Cricket Board.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:54.060
Now the fact is, in all of these leagues,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.180
Indian players who have
a global fan following

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.730
are not allowed to play, that's the rule.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.890
And if you can't get, you know,

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.470
the likes of MS Dhoni or Virat Kohli

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.480
or some of the other big boys that we have

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.310
playing cricket across the
world for their country

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.590
and in the IPL League,

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:13.140
I think you'll lose that many audiences.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.980
In an interview with ANI
Sports in August 2022,

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:20.190
the BCCI Vice President Rajiv Shukla

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.667
commented on the matter:

00:16:21.667 --> 00:16:24.967
"Our Indian Premier League
is itself a huge league

00:16:24.967 --> 00:16:26.947
and we cannot allow any of our players

00:16:26.947 --> 00:16:30.900
to attach themselves to any
foreign league in any manner."

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:33.510
The owners of the IPL teams
have found a clever way

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.583
to compete with these burgeoning leagues:

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.983
Buying the competition.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.730
All teams within South
Africa's new T20 tournament

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.850
have been bought by the
owners of IPL teams.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.770
There are 10 team owners in India.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.440
All of them have tasted
immense success in IPL.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.490
They've seen their evaluation

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.770
go from literally nothing to now

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.570
close to $2 billion per franchise

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.400
given the media rights valuation.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.380
When you taste that kind of success

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:01.170
in a limited timeframe of 10 or 15 years,

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:04.080
you certainly want to experiment
as an owner, a team owner,

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.513
and see what this can do
if other leagues take off.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:12.930
Now, non-cricketing countries,

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.480
seeing the opportunity that T20 brings,

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:18.090
are beginning to hedge their bets.

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:20.550
Not only is the shorter
format an easier game

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:21.750
to sell to those countries

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.670
with less understanding of the sport,

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.940
but the money floating around
and growing demand for talent

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.793
offers the perfect incentive
for young athletes.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.380
Right now, we're in the
middle of a historical event

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:36.780
for Cricket Finland
because we've never hosted

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.630
an international cricket
tournament before.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.980
But I think from our perspective,

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:43.550
as a nontraditional country,
we've been looking at,

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:44.610
at the data that's come out

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:46.860
from our World Cup qualifier event.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:49.140
There are quite significant
viewership figures

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:50.670
which have come through

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.763
purely from a Finnish-based viewership.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.810
And I think looking at that
in terms of the way forward,

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.851
that's come about simply because

00:17:59.851 --> 00:18:02.430
the game itself has become more attractive

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.870
for people to actually come and watch.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.540
It's become something which
is more sold as a product,

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.310
has more things going on for the viewer

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.720
when they come to the ground.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:11.250
We've tried to sort of mirror that here

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.270
with a very smaller version.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:15.090
Obviously we haven't got a
hundred thousand seater stadium

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:17.040
as they've got at a
traditional cricket ground

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.510
in India or England.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.940
But at the same time we have looked at it

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:22.980
to actually think about
how we can actually get

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.450
new people interested in the game

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.570
and have somebody at the
game that is referring

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:29.040
to what's actually happening
on the cricket field.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.343
for somebody that's never
seen a game a cricket before.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.050
For Finland,

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.020
a country whose own
national sport, Pesäpallo,

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:42.990
is also bat and ball-based, T20 offers

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:46.533
a potentially easy transition
for players and viewers.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.977
You only have to look at the
average salaries of Pesäpallo

00:18:49.977 --> 00:18:53.373
and IPL athletes to understand
the opportunity here.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:58.290
In 2019, the highest salary
for a Pesäpallo player

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.423
was about $55,000.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.650
That same year, the
IPL's top paid cricketer,

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.900
Virat Kohli's salary and winnings

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:08.823
came in at around $4 million.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.480
That's not to mention the $21 million

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.343
he banked through endorsements.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:18.300
The opportunities that are there for

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.070
players in nontraditional countries

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:23.040
to actually have access
to the the global stage,

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:26.070
whether that's IPL, whether
that's another franchise

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.390
somewhere else in the world,

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.920
or whether that's within the the

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:30.390
ICC'S Global Pathway events,

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.490
I think there's something which has

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:37.050
itself only developed in
the last five to 10 years.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:39.660
Every other cricket board internationally

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.490
is trying this format because

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:45.308
they think it'll result in
them getting a lot of largesse

00:19:45.308 --> 00:19:47.850
in terms of dollars that come in

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:50.910
and they can in turn improve
the local infrastructure

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.950
of the game in their respective countries,

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.900
which they probably can't do

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:56.370
given the current state of finances.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.620
So it's a chicken and egg situation.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.500
If they're able to successfully attract

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.590
and stage the first or second
season of the tournament

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.840
by attracting some world class players

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.670
and getting adequate consumers,

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.220
media companies will come
and follow those as well.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.810
Now cricket is hoping to break into

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:20.100
the largest sports market
in the world: The US.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.200
The US's Major League Cricket competition

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.240
is set to launch in 2023,

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.060
backed by investors such
as Bollywood superstar,

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.970
Shah Rukh Khan and Microsoft
Chairman Satya Nadella

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.230
The following year, in 2024,

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:36.990
Los Angeles will jointly
host the T20 World Cup

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:38.073
with the West Indies.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.950
And there's also a bid by the ICC

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:44.820
to feature cricket for the
first time ever in the Olympics,

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:47.940
which will also be in LA in 2028.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:50.940
With so much interest in
the sport and its expansion,

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:53.250
investors are picking
apart the business model

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:56.103
and exploring ways to
capitalize even further.

00:21:03.146 --> 00:21:05.580
It has now gone to serious business where

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:08.370
large business owners across the globe

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:12.060
are seeing this as an
opportunity to own a franchise,

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:13.833
probably improve governance,

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.530
get more independent sportsmen

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.090
to come on the boards of these companies

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.550
and therefore attract the
best talent, get sponsorships,

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.010
and increase the scale and
size of what they can do

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.633
in their respective franchises.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:29.100
Sport has become business
and sport is still run

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.050
and that is true beyond
cricket in other sports,

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:32.490
but particularly in cricket,

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.370
as if it's a cottage industry.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:37.770
We haven't got off the field,

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.640
the sort of leaders and
administrators we need

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:45.420
to run a big industry like this.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:48.390
An industry that appeals
to millions of people

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:52.020
and which can affect the
lives of millions of people

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:53.233
because for them it's

00:21:53.233 --> 00:21:55.233
a form of entertainment that they value.

